cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, data, or results, please cite it as below."
title: "How Far Can a PSRAM-less ESP32 Go? A TinyML Deployment Study for WiFi CSI HAR"
abstract: >-
  Code, executed notebook, on-device measurement firmware, results, and trained
  models for a deployment-characterization study of WiFi CSI human activity
  recognition on the classic PSRAM-less ESP32. Spans classical learners, tiny
  neural networks, and five deep architectures across UT-HAR and CSI-HAR, with
  measured on-device latency and memory on the classic ESP32.
type: software
